+        """Fit the material scale by weighted least squares.
+
+        Throughout the calibration interval both levels are in their
+        high-temperature phase for every allowed width.  The limiting mean
+        energy density is therefore ``-beta * width**2``.  Since the model is
+        linear in width squared, its unconstrained weighted least-squares
+        estimate has a closed form; the physical interval is imposed on that
+        estimate before taking its square root.
